<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.5.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00125</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.5.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>8dd1aed0-5aad-4649-873a-6fa766664159</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<para>Use the graph for questions 1 - 2.</para>
    <figure><media alt="graph of (0, 4) and (4, 0)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/aacd061405bc69664246ed8cf981961e9c6f1bb0"/></media></figure><list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
            <item>Which of the following ordered pairs are on the line? Select <emphasis>three</emphasis> answers.</item>
        </list>
        <list>
            <item>\((0, 4)\)</item>
            <item>\((-2, 6)\)</item>
            <item>\((-4, 0)\)</item>
            <item>\((2, 2)\)</item>
            <item>\((-1, 3)\)</item>
        </list>
        <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((0, 4)\), \((2, 2)\), \((-2, 6)\)</para>

        <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
            <item>Which of the following ordered pairs are solutions to the equation? Select <emphasis>three</emphasis> solutions.</item>
        </list>
        <list>
            <item>\((0, 4)\)</item>
            <item>\((-2, 6)\)</item>
            <item>\((-4, 0)\)</item>
            <item>\((2, 2)\)</item>
            <item>\((-1, 3)\)</item>
        </list>
        <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((0, 4)\), \((2, 2)\), \((-2, 6)\)</para>
<para>For questions 3 and 4, use the graph of y = 3x -1 as shown.</para>
<figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2552427885cd3a872ea3566334a685b3e8fd6171"/></media></figure><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
        <item>Which of the following ordered pairs are on the line? Select <emphasis>three</emphasis> answers</item>
    </list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>  \((0, -1)\), \((1, 2)\), \((2, 5)\)</para>

    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
        <item>Which of the following ordered pairs are solutions to the equation? Select <emphasis>three</emphasis> solutions.</item>
    </list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((0, -1)\), \((1, 2)\), \((2, 5)\)</para>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
        <item>Select <emphasis>three</emphasis> points that are on the graph of the equation \( 4y - 6x = 12 \).</item>
        <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b9f93f21031d9a609a1590b12847a90d908098d2"/></media></figure></list>
    <list>
        <item>\((-4, -3)\)</item>
        <item>\((-1, 1.5)\)</item>
        <item>\((0, -2)\)</item>
        <item>\((0, 3)\)</item>
        <item>\((3, -4)\)</item>
        <item>\((6, 4)\)</item>
    </list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((-4, -3)\), \((-1, 1.5)\), \((0, 3)\)</para>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
        <item>Here is a graph of the equation \( x+3y=6 \).</item>
    </list>
    <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4a347bae7c724f857dcffd3793112090bf5ce185"/></media></figure><para>Select <emphasis>three</emphasis> coordinate pairs that represent a solution to the equation.</para>
<list>
    <item> \((0, 2)\)</item>
    <item> \((6, 0)\)</item>
    <item> \((2, 6)\)</item>
    <item> \((3, 1)\)</item>
    <item> \((4, 1)\)</item>
    <item> \((6, 2)\)</item>
</list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((0, 2)\), \((3, 1)\), \((6, 0)\)</para>
    

</section>
</content>
</document>
